From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:33:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] spi: Apply GPIO chip-select delays only once
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

For a GPIO chip select, spi_set_cs() runs the cs_setup delay (on
assertion) or the cs_inactive delay (on deassertion) twice: once in
spi_toggle_csgpiod() for every GPIO it toggles, and once more at its own
end, where the same delays are handled for GPIO chip selects and for
controllers without programmable chip-select timing.

A device that asks for a 10 us setup time therefore gets 20 us, and one
with several GPIO chip selects gets the delay once per chip select plus
once more. Drop the delays from spi_toggle_csgpiod() so that they run
once, after every chip select has changed.

Boards that set these delays and use GPIO chip selects see their
effective delays halve.

Found while matching the iPad 5 (J71t) N1 touchscreen's chip-select
timing to iOS (J71t ledger 8.6).

Reported-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi.c | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi.c b/drivers/spi/spi.c
index 5b5b3bc5f..782cb74cf 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi.c
@@ -1252,11 +1252,6 @@ static void spi_toggle_csgpiod(struct spi_device *spi, u8 idx, bool enable, bool
 	else
 		/* Polarity handled by GPIO library */
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(spi_get_csgpiod(spi, idx), activate);
-
-	if (activate)
-		spi_delay_exec(&spi->cs_setup, NULL);
-	else
-		spi_delay_exec(&spi->cs_inactive, NULL);
 }
 
 static void spi_set_cs(struct spi_device *spi, bool enable, bool force)
@@ -1309,6 +1304,10 @@ static void spi_set_cs(struct spi_device *spi, bool enable, bool force)
 		spi->controller->set_cs(spi, !enable);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The delays run once, after every chip select has changed, including
+	 * when the chip select is a GPIO.
+	 */
 	if (spi_is_csgpiod(spi) || !spi->controller->set_cs_timing) {
 		if (activate)
 			spi_delay_exec(&spi->cs_setup, NULL);
